# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything is optional: with nothing set, the live lane records, detects,
# captions and stages clips in staging/ without logging in anywhere.
# One KEY=value per line, comments on their own lines: not every loader of this file (systemd, older
# scripts) cuts a "# comment" off the end of a value.
DRY_RUN=1
# From @BotFather; enables approval cards in the team chat.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Enables the Claude screen/judge (hooks, titles); heuristic fallback without it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Recordings and chat logs (NAS volume).
# CLIPWATCHER_DATA=/data/work
# Clip packages + clips.db. The live lane, the approval bot and the publisher must all see the same value.
# CLIPWATCHER_STAGING=/data/staging

# YouTube: Approve in Telegram uploads the Short. While DRY_RUN=1 nothing goes public.
# On a desktop (default, publish.youtube_mode: browser) there is nothing to set here: sign in once with
# `python scripts/yt_browser_login.py`; the Chrome profile is kept in ~/.clipwatcher/yt-chrome-profile.
# YT_BROWSER_PROFILE=~/.clipwatcher/yt-chrome-profile
# With DRY_RUN=1 the browser is not opened; YT_BROWSER_FORCE=1 uploads anyway, as private.
# YT_BROWSER_FORCE=1
# On a server without a display (Docker sets this itself, VPS): the Data API, with a token from
# scripts/youtube_auth.py (gitignored secrets/). With DRY_RUN=1 and a token it uploads as private.
# CLIPWATCHER_YOUTUBE_MODE=api
# YOUTUBE_CREDENTIALS=secrets/youtube_token.json
